{"author":{"id":"0fb62b7075a4219f84b4bf8c9c235af1632f3fa4b63ca899f025ad8215a930fd"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1778070109,"nonce":"fFkyfH0+Wrj+AdqBCXtoePJqa2s=","title":"Source-data author-name typos inflate n_authors after dedup","message":"Some theses have the same author spelled inconsistently across the source records (e.g. \"Ryland, Emil-André\" vs \"Ryland, Emil-Andé\" — missing 'r'). When deduplicate_masters() merges such rows, merge_authors() compares tokens by exact lowercase match, so it retains both spellings and n_authors is inflated by 1.\n\nCheapest fix: in merge_authors(), compare tokens after stripping diacritics + collapsing whitespace + dropping non-alphanumeric characters, and treat tokens within Levenshtein-1 of an already-seen token as duplicates. stringdist::stringdist() is the obvious dependency.\n\nLow priority — affects very few rows. Open this if downstream analysis cares about exact n_authors values.","files":null}]}